<title>CANADA: Noranda workers ratify contract - union.</title>
<headline>Noranda workers ratify contract - union.</headline>
<dateline>MIRAMICHI, New Brunswick 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unionized workers at Noranda Inc's Heath-Steele Mine have ratified a new collective agreement, union officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The three-year contract provides for wage increases and pension plan improvements, the United Steelworkers' of America said in a statement.</p>
<p>Steelworker staff representative Cal Luedee said the agreement &quot;will provide the necessary security and job improvements during a period of transition for the mine over the next few years.&quot; There are about 250 workers mining lead and zinc at Heath Steele site.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
